.TH FPUTC 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fputc \- write one byte to a Crunch stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int fputc(int " character ", struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes the low byte of
.I character
to the stream. The stream is unbuffered.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the written byte as an integer from 0 to 255, or
.B EOF
(\-1) on error with
.B errno
and the stream error indicator set. A null stream returns
.B EOF
with
.B errno
set to
.BR EINVAL .
.SH NOTES
Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fgetc (3crunch),
.BR fwrite (3crunch),
.BR stdout (3crunch),
.BR stderr (3crunch)
